Area and Volume 1|1.1|5252e606|372|C|mcq|-|The side length of a square is 55 cm. What is the area, in cm^2, of the square?|110;220;3025;12100|A=2s (doubled instead of squared); B=4s (perimeter); C=s^2 CORRECT; D=(2s)^2 (squared the doubled value)
Area and Volume 1|1.2|59cb654c|369|A|mcq|-|The area of a square is 64 square inches. What is the side length, in inches, of this square?|8;16;64;128|A=sqrt(A) CORRECT; B=A/4 (used perimeter relation); C=A itself (no operation); D=2A
Area and Volume 1|1.3|0837c3b9|476|B|mcq|-|Triangle ABC ~ triangle DEF, AB and DE corresponding. If DE=2AB and perimeter of ABC is 20, what is perimeter of DEF?|10;40;80;120|A=20/2 (inverted scale factor); B=20*2 CORRECT; C=20*4 (used area ratio k^2); D=20*6
Area and Volume 1|1.4|c88183f7|369|C|mcq|-|A rectangle has a length of 13 and a width of 6. What is the perimeter of the rectangle?|12;26;38;52|A=2w only; B=2l only; C=2(l+w) CORRECT; D=4l (treated as square on length)
Area and Volume 1|1.5|29e9b28c|660|A|mcq|triangle-3-sides-xyz|The triangle shown has a perimeter of 22 units. If x=9 and y=7 units, what is the value of z, in units?|6;7;9;16|A=22-9-7 CORRECT; B=y (copied a given); C=x (copied a given); D=x+y (added instead of subtracting from perimeter)
Area and Volume 1|1.6|3453aafc|397|D|mcq|-|What is the area, in square centimeters, of a rectangle with a length of 36 cm and a width of 34 cm?|70;140;1156;1224|A=l+w (added); B=2(l+w) (perimeter); C=34^2 (squared the width); D=l*w CORRECT
Area and Volume 1|1.7|f60bb551|394|A|mcq|-|The area of a rectangle is 630 square inches. The length is 70 inches. What is the width, in inches?|9;70;315;560|A=A/l CORRECT; B=l repeated; C=A/2 (halved area); D=A-70
Area and Volume 1|1.8|4420e500|369|B|mcq|-|What is the area of a rectangle with a length of 4 cm and a width of 2 cm?|6 cm^2;8 cm^2;12 cm^2;36 cm^2|A=l+w (added); B=l*w CORRECT; C=2(l+w) (perimeter); D=(l+w)^2 (perimeter squared)
Area and Volume 1|1.9|165c30c4|242|2048|spr|-|A rectangle has a length of 64 inches and a width of 32 inches. What is the area, in square inches?|-|SPR: 64*32=2048
