Linear Equations in Two Variables 1|1.16|520e6f5b|860|A|mcq|table-rock-types|In 0.03(120w)+0.18(180z)+3,385.80=7,576.20, the variable terms cover limestone and basalt. Best interpretation of 3,385.80?|Cost of granite and sandstone;Cost of basalt and limestone;Cost of basalt;Cost of sandstone|The constant covers the two rock types not represented by variables; A=CORRECT; B/C/D=name rock types already in the variable terms
