Linear Functions 2|2.1|e62cfe5f|291|2.6|spr|-|Head width in mm is 0.6 added to four times body weight in grams. What is the head width for a 0.5 gram bee?|-|SPR: 4(0.5)+0.6=2.6
Linear Functions 2|2.2|7e3f8363|397|C|mcq|-|The graph of linear function f contains (0,3) and (7,31). Which equation defines f?|f(x)=28x+34;f(x)=3x+38;f(x)=4x+3;f(x)=7x+3|Slope 28/7=4 with intercept 3; A=used the rise as the slope; B=swapped slope and intercept; D=used the run as the slope; C=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.3|620fe971|478|A|mcq|-|y=120-25x models tons of cargo remaining x hours after starting. Best interpretation of the x-intercept?|All cargo moved in about 4.8 hours;Moving about 4.8 tons per hour;Moving about 25 tons per hour;Started with 120 tons|The x-intercept is where y=0; B=misreads it as a rate; C=describes the slope; D=describes the y-intercept; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.4|5cf1bbc9|799|A|mcq|line-graph-video-games|A graph gives total cost for a game system and x games, with y-intercept 100 and reaching 350 at x=10. Best interpretation of the slope?|Each game costs 25 dollars;The system costs 100 dollars;The system costs 25 dollars;Each game costs 100 dollars|Slope is 250/10=25 per game; B=describes the intercept; C/D=swap slope and intercept; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.5|dae126d7|539|D|mcq|-|Boiling point is 212 F at sea level and drops 1 F per 550 feet. Which equation gives B at x feet?|B=550+x/212;B=550-x/212;B=212+x/550;B=212-x/550|Start at 212 and subtract x/550; A/B=swapped the constants; C=added instead of subtracting; D=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.6|271f7e3f|573|B|mcq|-|f(x)=(x+7)/4. What is the value of f(9)-f(1)?|1;2;1/4;9/4|16/4-8/4=2; A/C=subtracted before dividing; D=evaluated f(9) only; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.7|c651cc56|486|B|mcq|table-fx|A table gives f(0)=-2, f(2)=4, f(6)=16. What is the value of f(3)?|6;7;8;9|Slope 3 so f(x)=3x-2 and f(3)=7; A/C/D=interpolated by averaging adjacent rows; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.8|c22b5f25|480|C|mcq|-|The points (-2,3) and (4,-5) lie on the graph of which linear function?|f(x)=x+5;f(x)=(1/2)x+4;f(x)=-(4/3)x+1/3;f(x)=-(3/2)x+1|Slope is -8/6=-4/3 with intercept 1/3; A/B=positive slope; D=inverted the slope; C=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.9|11e1ab81|633|A|mcq|line-graph-conveyor|A graph of distance versus time passes through the origin and (3,6). Which equation relates d and m?|d=2m;d=(1/2)m;d=m+2;d=2m+2|Slope 2 through the origin; B=inverted the slope; C=used 2 as an intercept; D=added a nonzero intercept; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.10|4fe4fd7c|370|3500|spr|-|c(x)=mx+500 gives cost for x shirts. The cost for 100 shirts is 800 dollars. What is the cost for 1000 shirts?|-|SPR: m=3 so c(1000)=3500; error 8000 (scaled the total by 10)
Linear Functions 2|2.11|3122fc7b|263|257|spr|-|A linear model gives a population of 57 thousand in 1991 and 224 thousand in 2011. To the nearest whole number what is the value in 2015?|-|SPR: slope 8.35 per year so 57+24(8.35)=257.4 which rounds to 257
Linear Functions 2|2.12|c01f4a95|243|39|spr|-|j(x)=mx+144 and j(12)=18. What is the value of j(10)?|-|SPR: m=-10.5 so j(10)=-105+144=39
Linear Functions 2|2.13|868fc236|588|B|mcq|table-macronutrients|A table gives 4.0 food calories equal to 16.7 kilojoules. If x food calories equals k kilojoules, which best represents the relationship?|k=0.24x;k=4.2x;x=4.2k;xk=4.2|16.7/4.0 is about 4.2; A=inverted the ratio; C=solved for the wrong variable; D=made it a product; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.14|042aa429|369|C|mcq|-|If f(x)=x+7 and g(x)=7x, what is the value of 4f(2)-g(2)?|-5;1;22;28|4(9)-14=22; A/B=failed to distribute the 4; D=gave 4f(2) only; C=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.15|113b938e|575|C|mcq|-|y=18-5x gives bicycle speed x seconds after braking. Best interpretation of the x-coordinate of the x-intercept?|Speed before braking;Feet per second the speed decreased each second;Seconds until the bicycle stopped;Feet traveled until the bicycle stopped|The x-intercept is where speed reaches 0; A=describes the y-intercept; B=describes the slope; D=confuses time with distance; C=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.16|441558e7|442|A|mcq|-|y=0.67x+2.6 predicts larvae from x worker ants. For 58 worker ants which is closest to the predicted larvae?|41;61;83;190|0.67(58)+2.6=41.5; B=added 58 and 2.6; C/D=multiplied incorrectly; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.17|8a6de407|250|2|spr|-|f(x)=mx+b with f(0)=18 and f(1)=20. What is the value of m?|-|SPR: 20-18=2
Linear Functions 2|2.18|41fdc0b8|530|A|mcq|table-population|A table gives population 862 in 2000 and 846 in 2010. Which function models the population t years after 2000?|P(t)=862-1.6t;P(t)=862-16t;P(t)=862+16(t-2000);P(t)=862-1.6(t-2000)|Slope is -16/10=-1.6 and t is measured from 2000; B=used the ten-year change as the annual rate; C/D=subtracted 2000 again; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.19|1c29bfd1|441|A|mcq|-|Pressure is 14.70 psi at sea level and increases 0.44 psi per foot of descent. What is the pressure at 105 feet?|60.90;31.50;14.70;0.44|14.70+0.44(105)=60.90; B=used a wrong rate; C/D=copied a constant; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.20|295a41f0|875|B|mcq|line-graph-shifted|The graph of y=f(x)-11 has slope -2 and y-intercept -4. Which equation defines f?|f(x)=-13x-11;f(x)=-2x+7;f(x)=-13x+7;f(x)=-2x-11|Add 11 to the graphed intercept; A/C=added 11 to the slope; D=read the intercept directly; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.21|2f34cd1c|441|B|mcq|-|f(x)=55.20-0.16x gives surface water temperature on day x. What is the estimated temperature on day 326?|55.20;3.04;-0.16;-52.16|55.20-52.16=3.04; A=ignored the term; C=gave the slope; D=forgot to add 55.20; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.22|f0773a55|831|A|mcq|line-graph-electrician|A graph gives total charge for x hours with a onetime fee plus an hourly rate. Best interpretation of the slope?|The hourly rate;The onetime fee;The maximum charge;The total charge|Slope is the per-hour change; B=describes the intercept; C/D=describe outputs; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.23|23dedddd|372|D|mcq|-|For the linear function f, f(0)=8 and f(1)=12. Which equation defines f?|f(x)=12x+8;f(x)=4x;f(x)=4x+12;f(x)=4x+8|Slope 4 and intercept 8; A=used f(1) as the slope; B=dropped the intercept; C=used f(1) as the intercept; D=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.24|a775af14|397|C|mcq|-|The graph of linear function f contains (0,2) and (8,34). Which equation defines f?|f(x)=2x+42;f(x)=32x+36;f(x)=4x+2;f(x)=8x+2|Slope 32/8=4 with intercept 2; A=swapped slope and intercept; B=used the rise as the slope; D=used the run as the slope; C=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.25|b2fe7ab6|611|D|mcq|table-gx|A table gives g(1)=54, g(2)=51, g(3)=48, g(4)=45 for g(x)=mx+b. What is the value of b?|3;27;54;57|Slope -3 so b=g(0)=57; A=gave the absolute slope; C=gave g(1); B=misc; D=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.26|a91a2b75|243|9|spr|-|f(x)=-9x+9. What is the y-coordinate of the y-intercept of the graph of y=f(x)?|-|SPR: 9; error -9 (used the slope)
Linear Functions 2|2.27|af711d1b|611|C|mcq|table-distance-time|A table gives distance 0.32 km in 8 minutes, 0.56 in 14, 0.68 in 17. Which equation could represent this?|t=4d;t=(1/25)d;t=25d;t=(1/4)d|8/0.32=25; A/D=used a factor of 4; B=inverted the rate; C=CORRECT
Linear Functions 2|2.28|17d80dc3|219|7|spr|-|Line k has slope 5 and y-intercept (0,-35). What is the x-coordinate of the x-intercept?|-|SPR: 0=5x-35 so x=7
Linear Functions 3|3.1|2b15d65f|469|A|mcq|-|Demand was 20,000 units at 40 dollars and 15,000 units at 60 dollars. What is the demand at 55 dollars?|16250;16500;16750;17500|Slope -250 per dollar so 20000-250(15)=16250; B/C/D=used a wrong slope or wrong reference price; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.2|be9cb6a2|421|D|mcq|-|Renting a backhoe costs 270 dollars for the first day and 135 for each additional day. Which equation gives cost y for x days?|y=270x-135;y=270x+135;y=135x+270;y=135x+135|270+135(x-1)=135x+135; A/B=multiplied the first-day rate by all days; C=added the full first-day cost on top; D=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.3|b988eeec|244|-12|spr|-|f(x)=(1/4)x-9 and g(x)=(3/4)x+21. If h(x)=f(x)+g(x), what is the x-coordinate of the x-intercept of y=h(x)?|-|SPR: h(x)=x+12 so x=-12
Linear Functions 3|3.4|af2ba762|485|D|mcq|-|F(x)=2.74-0.19(x-3) gives average gas price x months after September 1. What does 2.74 estimate?|Average monthly decrease;Difference from September to December;Price on September 1;Price on December 1|The shift makes x=3 (December) give 2.74; A=describes the slope; B=describes a difference; C=wrong month; D=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.5|16889ef3|538|C|mcq|-|Production dropped from 4 million barrels in 2000 to 1.9 million in 2013. Which linear function models production t years after 2000?|f(t)=(21/130)t+4;f(t)=(19/130)t+4;f(t)=-(21/130)t+4;f(t)=-(19/130)t+4|Slope is -2.1/13=-21/130; A/B=positive slope; D=used 1.9 instead of the change; C=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.6|6989c80a|419|A|mcq|-|F(x)=(9/5)(x-273.15)+32 converts kelvins to Fahrenheit. If temperature increased 2.10 kelvins, what is the increase in Fahrenheit?|3.78;35.78;487.89;519.89|Only the slope matters for a change: (9/5)(2.10)=3.78; B=added 32; C/D=converted an absolute temperature; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.7|78391fcc|613|B|mcq|table-fx-negative|A table gives f(-11)=21, f(-10)=18, f(-9)=15, f(-8)=12. What is the x-intercept of y=f(x)?|(-3,0);(-4,0);(-9,0);(-12,0)|Slope -3 and intercept -12 so x=-4; A=gave the slope; C/D=read a table value; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.8|a04050d8|682|B|mcq|table-macronutrients|180 food calories come from p grams protein, f grams fat, c grams carbohydrate at 4, 9, 4 calories per gram. Which expresses f in terms of p and c?|f=20+(4/9)(p+c);f=20-(4/9)(p+c);f=20-(4/9)(p-c);f=20+(9/4)(p+c)|9f=180-4p-4c; A=sign error; C=sign error inside; D=inverted the fraction; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.9|daad7c32|486|D|mcq|-|The formula L=30+2w relates spring length in cm to weight in newtons. What does the 2 mean?|Length with no weight;Weight that stretches the spring 30 cm;Increase in weight per cm of length;Increase in length per newton of weight|The slope is cm per newton; A=describes the intercept; C=inverts the rate; D=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.10|023c0a8d|436|B|mcq|-|For the function f, f(3x)=x-6 for all x. What is the value of f(6)?|-6;-4;0;2|Set 3x=6 so x=2 and f(6)=-4; A=used x=0; C/D=solved for the wrong input; B=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.11|50f4cb9c|548|D|mcq|table-fx|A table gives f(1)=-64, f(2)=0, f(3)=64 for f(x)=ax+b. What is the value of a-b?|-64;62;128;192|a=64 and b=-128 so a-b=192; A=gave f(1); B/C=arithmetic slips; D=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.12|bbf9e5ce|421|A|mcq|-|A museum charges 21 dollars each for the first 25 people and 14 for each additional person. Which function gives the charge for n people, n at least 25?|f(n)=14n+175;f(n)=14n+525;f(n)=35n-350;f(n)=14n+21|21(25)+14(n-25)=14n+175; B=forgot to subtract the 25 at 14 dollars; C=added the rates; D=used 21 as a constant; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.13|b3abf40f|419|A|mcq|-|F(x)=(9/5)(x-273.15)+32. If temperature increased 9.10 kelvins, what is the increase in Fahrenheit?|16.38;48.38;475.29;507.29|(9/5)(9.10)=16.38; B=added 32; C/D=converted an absolute temperature; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.14|abcd0008|604|A|mcq|-|f(x)=6d(20x+21)+17. Which represents the x-intercept of the graph of y=f(x)+9, where d is a constant?|((-126d-26)/(120d),0);(9-(126d+17)/(120d),0);(-38/(120d+9),0);(126d+26,0)|Set 120dx+126d+26=0; B=failed to move the 9 correctly; C=added 9 to the coefficient; D=forgot to divide; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.15|a309803e|395|A|mcq|-|One gallon covers 220 square feet. A room has wall area w. Which equation gives paint P needed for two coats?|P=w/110;P=440w;P=w/220;P=220w|Two coats need 2w area so P=2w/220=w/110; C=one coat only; B/D=multiplied instead of dividing; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.16|0bd33265|272|515|spr|-|h=9(v-273.15)/5+32 converts kelvins to Fahrenheit. If a substance is 467.33 F, what is its temperature in kelvins?|-|SPR: 435.33=1.8(v-273.15) so v=515
Linear Functions 3|3.17|a7e2859a|411|A|mcq|-|Renting a canopy tent costs 430 dollars for the first day and 215 for each additional day. Which equation gives cost y for x days?|y=215x+215;y=430x-215;y=430x+215;y=215x+430|430+215(x-1)=215x+215; B/C=multiplied the first-day rate by all days; D=added the full first-day cost; A=CORRECT
Linear Functions 3|3.18|0b0fa68b|219|2/43|spr|-|For the function f, f(cx)=x-8 for all x, c positive. If f(2)=35, what is the value of c?|-|SPR: 2/c-8=35 so 2/c=43 and c=2/43
Linear Functions 3|3.19|e25f0807|369|16.25|spr|table-two-points|A table gives (-12,-45) and (6,45). The line passes through (1/4,a). What is a?|-|SPR: slope 5 and intercept 15 so a=1.25+15=16.25
Linear Inequalities 2|2.1|f224df07|466|C|mcq|-|A helicopter carries 100-pound and 120-pound packages, at least 10 packages, total weight at most 1,100 pounds. What is the maximum number of 120-pound packages?|2;4;5;6|With 10 packages 1000+20b<=1100 gives b<=5; D=ignored the minimum count; A/B=understated; C=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.2|b1228811|830|B|mcq|system-of-inequalities|At least 10 staff; juniors 640 per week and seniors 880; budget at most 9,700; at least 3 juniors and 1 senior. Which system represents this?|640x+880y>=9700 with x+y<=10;640x+880y<=9700 with x+y>=10 and x>=3 and y>=1;budget >= with x<=3;budget <= with x+y<=10|B=CORRECT; A=reversed both the budget and count signs; C/D=reversed the minimum staffing constraints
Linear Inequalities 2|2.3|64c85440|518|D|mcq|-|Parking spaces are at least 7.5 and at most 9.0 feet wide along a 135-foot curb. Which describes all possible values of n?|18<=n<=135;7.5<=n<=9;15<=n<=135;15<=n<=18|135/9=15 and 135/7.5=18; A/C=used the curb length as a bound; B=copied the widths; D=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.4|968e9e51|492|D|mcq|system-of-inequalities|Which ordered pair is a solution to y<=x and y<=-x?|(1,0);(-1,0);(0,1);(0,-1)|Need y at or below both lines; A/B satisfy only one; C fails both; D=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.5|bf5f80c6|395|A|mcq|-|Which point (x,y) is a solution to y<-4x+4?|(-4,0);(0,5);(2,1);(2,-1)|0<20 is true; B/C/D=fail the inequality; A=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.6|80da233d|472|D|mcq|-|An elephant weighs 200 pounds at birth and gains more than 2 but less than 3 pounds per day. Which inequality gives possible weights after 365 days?|400<w<600;565<w<930;730<w<1095;930<w<1295|200+365(2)=930 and 200+365(3)=1295; C=omitted the birth weight; A/B=used wrong rates; D=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.7|b31c3117|559|A|mcq|-|H=120p+60 with p between 0.5 and 0.85. Which inequality describes the target training heart rate?|120<=H<=162;102<=H<=120;60<=H<=162;60<=H<=102|Substitute both endpoints; C/D=used p=0 as a bound; B=misc; A=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.8|e9ef0e6b|420|B|mcq|-|Whales travel 72 to 77 miles per day. Which inequality gives total miles x in 16 days?|72+16<=x<=77+16;(72)(16)<=x<=(77)(16);72<=16+x<=77;72<=16x<=77|Multiply the daily range by 16; A/C=added instead; D=put the multiplier on the wrong side; B=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.9|90bd9ef8|538|B|mcq|-|Annual energy cost is 4,334 dollars, dropping to 2,712 after a 25,000 dollar install. Which inequality finds t where savings exceed the cost?|25000>(4334-2712)t;25000<(4334-2712)t;25000-4334>2712t;25000>(4332/2712)t|Savings per year times t must exceed 25,000; A=reversed; C/D=malformed; B=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.10|948087f2|585|D|mcq|system-of-inequalities|Which ordered pair satisfies y<=3x+1 and x-y>1?|(-2,-1);(-1,3);(1,5);(2,-1)|(2,-1) gives -1<=7 and 3>1; A/B/C=fail one inequality; D=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.11|34aca984|417|A|mcq|-|A rectangle has length 50 inches and width x inches with perimeter at most 210. Which inequality represents this?|2x+100<=210;2x+100>=210;2x+50<=210;2x+50>=210|Perimeter is 2x+100; B/D=reversed the sign; C=used 50 not 100; A=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.12|f02b4509|418|A|mcq|-|A truck tows at most 4,600 pounds. The trailer weighs 500 pounds and each box 120. What is the maximum number of boxes?|34;35;38;39|120n<=4100 gives n<=34.17; B=rounded up past the cap; C/D=ignored the trailer weight; A=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.13|6daf8d70|602|D|mcq|system-of-inequalities|No more than 164 bushes total and azaleas at most three times boxwoods. Which system represents this?|a+b>=164 and 3a>=b;a+b>=164 and a<=3b;a+b<=164 and 3a>=b;a+b<=164 and a<=3b|D=CORRECT; A/B=reversed the total constraint; A/C=attached the 3 to the wrong variable
Linear Inequalities 2|2.14|0ef4a7b6|432|A|mcq|-|A plant is tall if its height exceeds 100 cm. Which inequality represents possible heights for a tall species?|106<h<158;80<h<100;42<h<87;17<h<85|Every value in the interval must exceed 100; B/C/D=include values at or below 100; A=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 2|2.15|6cb9bf45|953|D|mcq|table-choices|For which table are all values of x and y solutions to y>7x-4?|x 3,5,8 with y 13,27,48;y 17,31,52;y 21,27,52;y 21,35,56|Each y must exceed 7x-4; D=all three satisfy CORRECT; A/B/C=at least one row fails
Linear Inequalities 2|2.16|b78cd5df|303|25|spr|-|A venue costs a onetime 35 dollars plus 10.25 per attendee with a 300 dollar budget. What is the greatest number of attendees?|-|SPR: 10.25n<=265 gives n<=25.85 so 25
Linear Inequalities 3|3.1|45cfb9de|492|D|mcq|-|Walking takes 20 minutes; the bus takes 5 minutes plus a wait of w minutes. Which inequality gives w for which walking is faster?|w-5<20;w-5>20;w+5<20;w+5>20|Walking is faster when the bus total exceeds 20; C=reversed; A/B=subtracted the ride time; D=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.2|95cad55f|700|A|mcq|system-of-inequalities|Detergent weighs 7.35 lb and softener 6.2 lb, shipment at most 300 lb, at least twice as many detergent containers. Which system represents this?|7.35d+6.2s<=300 and d>=2s;7.35d+6.2s<=300 and 2d>=s;14.7d+6.2s<=300 and d>=2s;14.7d+6.2s<=300 and 2d>=s|A=CORRECT; B/D=put the 2 on the wrong side; C/D=doubled the detergent weight
Linear Inequalities 3|3.3|ee2f611f|315|28|spr|-|A monthly pass is 95 dollars; individual tickets cost 1.50, 2.50, or 3.50. What is the minimum number of trips for which the pass could cost less?|-|SPR: 95<3.50n gives n>27.14 so 28 (uses the most expensive fare since the pass only needs to be cheaper in some case)
Linear Inequalities 3|3.4|6c71f3ec|450|B|mcq|-|Earnings are base salary x plus 11 percent commission on sales s, with total between 3x and 4x. Which inequality gives possible s?|2x<=s<=3x;(2/0.11)x<=s<=(3/0.11)x;3x<=s<=4x;(3/0.11)x<=s<=(4/0.11)x|Commission must fall between 2x and 3x so divide by 0.11; A/C=forgot to divide; D=forgot to subtract the base; B=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.5|1a621af4|239|-14|spr|-|A number x is at most 2 less than 3 times y. If y is -4, what is the greatest possible value of x?|-|SPR: x<=3(-4)-2=-14
Linear Inequalities 3|3.6|1035faea|594|D|mcq|-|Of 300 participants, 36 of the first 150 chose the first picture and p of the remaining 150 did. If more than 20 percent chose it, which inequality describes p?|p>0.20(300-36) with p<=150;p>0.20(300+36) with p<=150;p-36>0.20(300) with p<=150;p+36>0.20(300) with p<=150|Total choosers is p+36 and must exceed 60; A/B=adjusted the population instead; C=subtracted; D=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.7|5bf5136d|418|C|mcq|-|A triangle has sides 6 and 12. Which inequality represents possible lengths x of the third side?|x<18;x>18;6<x<18;x<6 or x>18|The third side lies strictly between the difference and the sum; A/B=kept one bound; D=inverted the interval; C=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.8|e8f9e117|399|20|spr|-|I=V/R with R=500 ohms and V=6n volts from n six-volt batteries. If current is at most 0.25 ampere, what is the greatest n?|-|SPR: 6n/500<=0.25 gives n<=20.83 so 20
Linear Inequalities 3|3.9|963da34c|578|A|mcq|-|Base perimeter plus height cannot exceed 130 inches. Height is 60 and length is 2.5 times width x. Which inequality shows allowable x?|0<x<=10;0<x<=11 2/3;0<x<=17 1/2;0<x<=20|2(x+2.5x)+60<=130 gives 7x<=70; B/C/D=mis-computed the base perimeter; A=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.10|b8e73b5b|491|C|mcq|-|Ken earned 8 dollars per hour for 10 hours then 10 per hour, saving 90 percent. What is the least number of additional hours to save at least 270 dollars?|38;33;22;16|0.9(80+10h)>=270 gives h>=22; D=ignored the savings rate; A/B=used a wrong base; C=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.11|830120b0|552|B|mcq|system-of-inequalities|Which consists of the y-coordinates of all points satisfying y>2x-1 and 2x>5?|y>6;y>4;y>5/2;y>3/2|Substituting 2x>5 gives y>5-1=4; A=used 2x>7; C=gave the bound on x; D=halved; B=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.12|68c5c81a|436|C|mcq|-|11x+14y<=115 models spending at most 115 dollars on x small and y large pizzas. Best interpretation of 14y?|Amount spent on each large pizza;Amount spent on each small pizza;Total amount spent on large pizzas;Total amount spent on small pizzas|14y is price times quantity for large pizzas; A=describes 14 alone; B/D=wrong size; C=CORRECT
Linear Inequalities 3|3.13|f8ff3249|994|C|mcq|table-choices|For which table are all values of x and y solutions to y<6x+2?|x 3,5,7 with y 20,32,44;y 16,36,40;y 16,28,40;y 24,36,48|Each y must be below 6x+2; C=all three satisfy CORRECT; A/B/D=at least one row fails
Linear Inequalities 3|3.14|55ea82f3|499|B|mcq|-|At least 140 tickets before the event and 220 during, raising at least 5,820 dollars. During-event price x is 3 dollars less than before. Which inequality represents this?|140(x+3)+220x<=5820;140(x+3)+220x>=5820;140(x-3)+220x<=5820;140(x-3)+220x>=5820|Before-price is x+3 and the total is at least 5,820; A/C=reversed the sign; C/D=subtracted from the wrong price; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 1|1.13|36200a38|464|B|mcq|triangle-sides-extended|Two sides of a triangle are extended past the apex; base angles are 70 and 50 degrees. What is the value of x, the angle between the extensions?|110;120;130;140|Apex angle is 60 so the labeled adjacent angle is 120; A/C/D=added or subtracted the base angles incorrectly; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 1|1.14|69f4bbdc|764|B|mcq|right-triangle-13|A right triangle has one acute angle of 13 degrees. What is the value of a, the other acute angle?|13;77;90;103|Acute angles are complementary; A=copied the given; C=the right angle; D=added 90; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 1|1.15|f1747a6a|393|D|mcq|-|In triangle ABC, angle B is 52 degrees and angle C is 17 degrees. What is the measure of angle A?|21;35;69;111|180-52-17=111; C=added the two given; B=subtracted them; A=misc; D=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 1|1.16|3b4b5b1e|543|47|spr|parallel-lines-133|Line j is parallel to line k and a transversal makes a 133 degree angle adjacent to x on line j. What is the value of x?|-|SPR: supplementary so 180-133=47
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 1|1.17|5207e508|699|D|mcq|parallel-lines-170|Line m is parallel to line n and a transversal makes a 170 degree angle at m. What is the value of w at n?|17;30;70;170|Corresponding angles are equal; A/B/C=took a supplement or a difference; D=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 1|1.18|e0d2e21a|652|C|mcq|two-triangles-dilation|Triangle ABC with angle A of 60 degrees is dilated by a scale factor of 3 to obtain XYZ, where d=16. What is the measure of angle X?|20;57;60;63|Dilation preserves angle measures; A/B/D=scaled or adjusted the angle; C=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 1|1.19|9d078710|867|A|mcq|parallel-lines-proof|Line l intersects lines j and k with a 40 degree angle marked at k and w, x at j and y, z at k. Which additional fact proves j is parallel to k?|w=40;x=140;y=40;z=140|Corresponding angles equal proves parallel; B/C/D=describe angles that are already determined or do not force parallelism; A=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.1|81b664bc|584|B|mcq|trapezoid-parallel-segments|AF, BE, and CD are parallel with B on AC and E on FD. AB=9, BC=18.5, FE=8.5. What is the length of ED to the nearest tenth?|16.8;17.5;18.4;19.6|Proportion 9/18.5=8.5/ED gives 17.47; A/C/D=inverted or mis-set the proportion; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.2|94364a79|418|B|mcq|-|A 10-foot tree casts a 5-foot shadow. Another tree casts a 2-foot shadow. How tall is the other tree?|3;4;8;27|Ratio 10/5=2 so height is 4; A/C=mis-scaled; D=multiplied incorrectly; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.3|933fee1a|616|B|mcq|two-right-triangles-32-58|Triangle ABC has angle A of 32 degrees with a right angle at C; DEF has angle D of 58 degrees with a right angle at F. Which ratio equals BC over AB?|DE/DF;DF/DE;DF/EF;EF/DE|BC/AB is sin 32 which equals DF/DE in DEF; A=inverted; C/D=used the wrong pair of sides; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.4|a4c05a1b|731|B|mcq|parallel-lines-r-s|Lines r and s are parallel and line m crosses both. If y<65, which must be true?|x<115;x>115;x+y<180;x+y>180|x and y are supplementary so x=180-y and y<65 gives x>115; C/D=misstate the sum; A=reversed; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.5|d3fe472f|418|D|mcq|-|Triangle ABC is similar to XYZ with each side of XYZ twice the corresponding side of ABC. AB is 16. What is the measure of XY?|14;16;18;32|Multiply by the scale factor; B=copied AB; A/C=added or subtracted; D=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.6|fd8745fc|242|84|spr|-|In triangle JKL, angles K and L each measure 48 degrees. What is the measure of angle J, in degrees?|-|SPR: 180-96=84
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.7|901e3285|426|D|mcq|-|In triangle ABC angle A is 50 degrees and the triangle is isosceles. Which is NOT a possible measure of angle B?|50;65;80;100|50, 65, and 80 each allow a pair of equal angles; 100 leaves 30 with no pair equal; D=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.8|1c3d613c|414|20|spr|two-triangles-ratio-3|Triangles ABC and DEF have AB/DE=BC/EF=AC/DF=3. If angle BAC is 20 degrees, what is the measure of angle EDF?|-|SPR: similarity preserves angles so 20; error 60 (multiplied by the scale factor)
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.9|6dd463ca|574|B|mcq|triangle-BD-parallel-AE|Segments AE and BD are parallel. Angle BDC is 58 degrees and angle ACE is 62 degrees. What is the measure of angle CAE?|58;60;62;120|Angle AEC equals 58 by corresponding angles so angle CAE is 180-62-58=60; A/C=copied a given; D=doubled; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.10|7a8ad237|243|21|spr|-|Triangles ABC and DEF are congruent with A corresponding to D and B and E right angles. Angle A is 69 degrees. What is the measure of angle F?|-|SPR: 180-90-69=21
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.11|014edcb7|670|B|mcq|triangle-PQR-extended|In triangle PQR, QR is extended to S. Angle PQR is 132 degrees and angle PRS is 163 degrees. What is the measure of angle QPR?|48;31;24;17|Angle PRQ is 17 so angle QPR is 180-132-17=31; D=gave angle PRQ; A/C=used supplements incorrectly; B=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.12|2085e10e|432|D|mcq|-|Triangle DEF has angles 47 and 97 degrees; triangle RST has angles 47 and 97 degrees. What additional information determines whether DEF is similar to RST?|Measure of angle F;Measure of angle T;Measures of angles F and T;No additional information is needed|Two pairs of equal angles already guarantee similarity; A/B/C=request redundant information; D=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 2|2.13|2f7c92ad|759|C|mcq|triangle-CAE-CBD|Triangle CAE is similar to triangle CBD, angle CBD is 57 degrees, and AE=26(BD). What is the measure of angle CAE?|(26*57);(26+57);57;26|Similarity preserves angle measure regardless of the scale factor; A/B=applied the factor to the angle; D=used the factor itself; C=CORRECT
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 3|3.1|6d99b141|576|83|spr|triangle-AC-CD-isosceles|In the figure AC=CD, angle EBC is 45 degrees, and angle ACD is 104 degrees. What is the value of x?|-|SPR: base angles are 38 so angle BED=97 and x=83
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 3|3.2|e10d8313|530|123|spr|figure-PV-RU-SX|Q, R, S, T lie on PV and RU meets SX at W. Angle SQX is 48, SXQ is 86, SWU is 85, VTU is 162 degrees. What is the measure of angle TUR?|-|SPR: chain gives angle TRU=39 and angle RTU=18 so angle TUR=123
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 3|3.3|f88f27e5|340|97|spr|three-intersecting-lines|Intersecting lines r, s, and t are shown with angles 106 and 23 degrees marked. What is the value of x?|-|SPR: exterior angle gives 74+23=97
Lines, Angles, and Triangles 3|3.4|947a3cde|379|30|spr|MQ-NR-intersect|MQ and NR intersect at P with NP=QP and MP=PR. Angles 70 and 60 degrees are marked. What is the measure of angle QMR?|-|SPR: angle MPR=120 and MP=PR so the base angles are 30
