Lines, Angles, and Triangles 3|3.16|fecc446d|433|A|mcq|-|A transversal crosses two parallel lines; one of the eight angles is (7x-250) degrees. The sum of four of the eight is k degrees. Which could NOT equal k?|-14x+1540;14x-320;-28x+1720;360|Achievable sums are 28x-1000, 14x-320, 360, -14x+1040, and -28x+1720; A gives 1540 not 1040 so it is impossible; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 1|1.9|98f735f2|512|B|mcq|-|T=PQ gives total revenue from price P and quantity Q. Which equation gives Q in terms of P and T?|Q=P/T;Q=T/P;Q=PT;Q=T-P|Divide both sides by P; A=inverted; C/D=multiplied or subtracted; B=CORRECT
