Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.1|fc3d783a|243|6|spr|-|A line 2y=4.5 meets the parabola y=-4x^2+bx at exactly one point, b positive. What is the value of b?|-|SPR: discriminant b^2-36=0 so b=6
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.2|4661e2a9|476|A|mcq|-|For the system x-y=1 and x+y=x^2-3, which ordered pair is a solution?|(1+sqrt3,sqrt3);(sqrt3,-sqrt3);(1+sqrt5,sqrt5);(sqrt5,-1+sqrt5)|Substituting gives x^2-2x-2=0 so x=1+sqrt3 and y=sqrt3; C/D=used the wrong discriminant; B=swapped; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.3|f65288e8|602|A|mcq|-|If 1/(x^2+10x+25)=4, which is a possible value of x+5?|1/2;5/2;9/2;11/2|The denominator is (x+5)^2 so (x+5)^2=1/4 and x+5=1/2 or -1/2; B/C/D=solved for x instead; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.4|f2f3fa00|350|5|spr|-|a=(vf-12)/5 gives average acceleration. Rewritten as vf=xa+y, what is the value of x?|-|SPR: vf=5a+12 so x=5
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.5|6ce95fc8|540|D|mcq|-|Which is a solution to 2x^2-2=2x+3?|2;1-sqrt11;(1/2)+sqrt11;(1+sqrt11)/2|2x^2-2x-5=0 gives x=(1+-sqrt11)/2; B/C=dropped the division by 2; A=guess; D=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.6|c303ad23|217|5|spr|-|If 3x^2-18x-15=0, what is the value of x^2-6x?|-|SPR: divide by 3 to get x^2-6x-5=0 so x^2-6x=5
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.7|7bd10ef3|454|A|mcq|-|2x^2-4x=t has no real solutions. Which could be the value of t?|-3;-1;1;3|Discriminant 16+8t<0 requires t<-2; B/C/D=values that give real roots; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.8|66bce0c1|460|B|mcq|-|What is the solution set of sqrt(2x+6)+4=x+3?|{-1};{5};{-1,5};{0,-1,5}|Squaring gives x^2-4x-5=0 but x=-1 is extraneous; A=kept only the extraneous root; C/D=failed to check; B=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.9|97e50fa2|492|2, 8|spr|graph-parabola|f(x)=-(1/2)(x-4)^2+10 and g(x)=-x+10. What is one possible value of a such that f(a)=g(a)?|-|SPR: x^2-10x+16=0 so x=2 or 8; both accepted
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.10|3d12b1e0|242|-1|spr|-|-16x^2-8x+c=0 has exactly one solution. What is the value of c?|-|SPR: discriminant 64+64c=0 so c=-1
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.11|71014fb1|393|D|mcq|-|How many distinct real solutions does (x-1)^2=-4 have?|Exactly one;Exactly two;Infinitely many;Zero|A square cannot equal a negative number; A/B=ignored the sign; D=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.12|e9349667|491|D|mcq|-|For y=x^2+2x+1 and x+y+1=0 with solutions (x1,y1) and (x2,y2), what is y1+y2?|-3;-2;-1;1|Roots x=-1 and -2 give y=0 and 1 so the sum is 1; A/B/C=summed the x values or mis-signed; D=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.13|b03adde3|517|D|mcq|-|If u-3=6/(t-2), what is t in terms of u?|t=1/u;t=(2u+9)/u;t=1/(u-3);t=2u/(u-3)|Invert then add 2 and combine; A/C=forgot the 2; B=wrong numerator; D=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.14|30281058|430|A|mcq|-|The graph of y=x^2-9 meets line p at (1,a) and (5,b). What is the slope of line p?|6;2;-2;-6|a=-8 and b=16 so the slope is 24/4=6; D=sign error; B/C=used a wrong run; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.15|5910bfff|597|A|mcq|-|D=T-(9/25)(100-H) approximates dew point. Which expresses H in terms of T and D?|H=(25/9)(D-T)+100;H=(25/9)(D-T)-100;H=(25/9)(D+T)+100;H=(25/9)(D+T)-100|Isolate 100-H then solve; B=sign error on 100; C/D=added T instead of subtracting; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.16|1697ffcf|253|5|spr|-|The graph of y=3x^2-14x meets y=x at (0,0) and (a,a). What is the value of a?|-|SPR: 3x^2-15x=0 so a=5
