Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.18|2c5c22d0|449|C|mcq|-|How many solutions are there to the system y=x^2+3x-7 and y-5x+8=0?|Exactly 4;Exactly 2;Exactly 1;None|Setting equal gives (x-1)^2=0 which is a repeated root; B=assumed two crossings; D=assumed none; C=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.19|fc3dfa26|564|C|mcq|-|What value of x satisfies 4x^2/(x^2-9)-2x/(x+3)=1/(x-3)?|-3;-1/2;1/2;3|Clearing denominators gives (2x-1)(x+3)=0; x=-3 is excluded so x=1/2; A/D=excluded values; B=sign error; C=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.20|58b109d4|268|-10|spr|-|For the system x^2+y+7=7 and 20x+100-y=0, what is the value of x?|-|SPR: -x^2=20x+100 gives (x+10)^2=0 so x=-10
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.21|7028c74f|224|31/3|spr|-|What is the sum of the solutions to 5(x+7)=15(x-17)(x+7)?|-|SPR: roots are -7 and 52/3 so the sum is 31/3
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.22|e11294f9|245|31|spr|-|Solutions to x^2+6x+7=0 are r<s and to x^2+8x+8=0 are t<u. If x^2+14x+c=0 has solutions r+t and s+u, what is c?|-|SPR: product (-7-3sqrt2)(-7+3sqrt2)=49-18=31
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.23|f5aa5040|243|20.25|spr|-|A line 2y=c meets the parabola y=-2x^2+9x at exactly one point. What is the value of c?|-|SPR: discriminant 81-4c=0 so c=20.25
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.24|7dbd46d9|442|A|mcq|-|The graphs of 8x+y=-11 and 2x^2=y+341 intersect at (x,y). What is a possible value of x?|-15;-11;2;8|Substituting gives x^2+4x-165=0 so x=-15 or 11; B=copied a constant; C/D=not roots; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.25|6011a3f8|418|A|mcq|-|64x^2+bx+25=0. For which value of b does the equation have more than one real solution?|-91;-80;5;40|Need b^2>6400 so absolute value of b exceeds 80; B=gives exactly one; C/D=too small; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.26|77c0cced|442|C|mcq|-|For y=2x^2-21x+64 and y=3x+a intersecting at exactly one point, what is the value of x?|-8;-6;6;8|Discriminant zero gives a=-8 and then x=6; A=gave a; B/D=sign or arithmetic slips; C=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 3|3.27|3a9d60b2|242|9|spr|-|2 times the absolute value of (4-x) plus 3 times the same equals 25. What is the positive solution?|-|SPR: 5 times the absolute value equals 25 so 4-x=5 or -5 giving x=-1 or 9
